Package: cmp50hx-unlock
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: xrip <xrip@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/xrip/cmp50hx-unlock
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Depends: dkms, build-essential, patch, kmod, pciutils, python3, mokutil, efibootmgr, initramfs-tools, linux-headers-generic | linux-headers-cloud-amd64 | linux-headers-amd64
Conflicts: nvidia-driver, nvidia-settings
Description: CMP 50HX compute unlock for Ubuntu (NVIDIA 610.43.03 + patched open modules)
 One-click unlock for the NVIDIA CMP 50HX (TU102, 10de:1e09). The package
 embeds the official NVIDIA 610.43.03 .run and installs its userland,
 ships the patched open kernel modules as a DKMS tree (stock-flow GSP
  compute unlock, ReBAR, PCIe Gen2, profiling counters) that rebuilds
  automatically on every kernel update, deploys the UEFI ESP unlock
  binary, and installs the cmp50hx-boot boot-flow service (unlock
  verdict, PCIe Gen2 retrain as a GPU readiness gate), the idle
  P-state governor (enabled by default) and the cmp-tune utility.
 .
 Removing this package uninstalls the NVIDIA driver it embedded.
 Supported: Ubuntu 24.04 / 26.04 amd64 (the 26.04 install path is
 gated in CI by an ubuntu:26.04 container that installs the published
 .deb and builds the DKMS tree against the 26.04 kernel headers).
